# Become Chaotic Neutral by the ordinary "Issue Request" command, as a
# Neutral character who has stated a Chaotic desired alignment. This is the
# treachery half of bd inc-r6ae; tools/check_align_treachery_play.sh reads it.
#
# WHAT IS BEING OBSERVED. Character::AlignedAct (src/Prayer.cpp) moves the
# law/chaos score (alignLC) on a Chaotic act and must set AL_CHAOTIC once that
# score passes +20 -- exactly as its good/evil twin sets AL_EVIL. Before the fix
# the else branch that sets the flag was missing AND a Neutral character's
# Chaotic act moved alignLC the WRONG WAY (-=, toward Lawful); the score could
# never reach +20, the alignment never changed and the game never printed
# "You are now ...". This run prints it.
#
# THE CHARACTER is the fixture elf-rogue-bluff-seed1-opt0822 (INCURSION_LOAD),
# an elf rogue whose skill ranks went to skills other than Bluff's rivals, so
# Bluff +7 outranks both Intimidate +5 and Diplomacy +5. This script starts in
# the dungeon, with that character already loaded. Creature::Request (src/Social.cpp:1184-1192) checks Intimidate
# first and Bluff second: with Intimidate not greater than Diplomacy, and Bluff
# greater, it offers "Use Bluff?" and fires the TREACHERY aligned act
# (AL_NONLAWFUL|AL_CHAOTIC, magnitude 3). An ORC cannot be used here: the orc
# race grants Intimidate as a racial skill (lib/races.irh:1867) and +4 Strength,
# so an orc's Intimidate outscores its Diplomacy and the game always offers
# Intimidate, never Bluff. An elf has neither Intimidate nor Bluff as a racial
# skill (lib/races.irh:1124).
#
# THE DESIRED ALIGNMENT is stated with the character sheet's own
# '[D] Alignment' command (src/Managers.cpp:2315-2322) and set to Chaotic
# Neutral. Without it AlignedAct clamps the score back to zero as a designed
# guard.
#
# THE VICTIM is a human conjured by wizard mode, one square east, and frozen.
# Wizard mode sets up state a player could reach; every coercion below is the
# ordinary command. Elf rogues start hiding, so the first request answers a
# "Confirm reveal yourself by talking?" prompt; the guard covers it and is
# harmless once it stops appearing.
#
# THE COUNT. alignLC starts at 0 and each treachery adds 3, so the +20 threshold
# is crossed on the seventh (alignLC = 21). Eight are sent for margin.
#
# Determinism: the fixture's character and map; options tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat.

s                       # one real turn; without it the first "d" did not open the sheet (observed)
d
@until "Desired Alignment" D
@choose "Chaotic Neutral"
ESC

w
y
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
@expect "Freeze Monsters"
DOWN*10
@expect "all monsters are denied their"
SPACE
@expect "Wizard Mode Options"
ESC
@dump:frozen

w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Humans"
@choose "human"
RIGHT ENTER
@dump:summoned

y
@choose "Issue Request"
RIGHT ENTER
@while "Confirm reveal yourself" y
@while "Use Bluff?" y
@dump:coerce1
@choose "Go To Location"
ESC

y
@choose "Issue Request"
RIGHT ENTER
@while "Confirm reveal yourself" y
@while "Use Bluff?" y
@dump:coerce2
@choose "Go To Location"
ESC

y
@choose "Issue Request"
RIGHT ENTER
@while "Confirm reveal yourself" y
@while "Use Bluff?" y
@dump:coerce3
@choose "Go To Location"
ESC

y
@choose "Issue Request"
RIGHT ENTER
@while "Confirm reveal yourself" y
@while "Use Bluff?" y
@dump:coerce4
@choose "Go To Location"
ESC

y
@choose "Issue Request"
RIGHT ENTER
@while "Confirm reveal yourself" y
@while "Use Bluff?" y
@dump:coerce5
@choose "Go To Location"
ESC

y
@choose "Issue Request"
RIGHT ENTER
@while "Confirm reveal yourself" y
@while "Use Bluff?" y
@dump:coerce6
@choose "Go To Location"
ESC

y
@choose "Issue Request"
RIGHT ENTER
@while "Confirm reveal yourself" y
@while "Use Bluff?" y
@dump:coerce7
@choose "Go To Location"
ESC

y
@choose "Issue Request"
RIGHT ENTER
@while "Confirm reveal yourself" y
@while "Use Bluff?" y
@dump:coerce8
@choose "Go To Location"
ESC

v
@dump:messages
ESC

d
@dump:sheet-after
ESC
@quit
